{"chunk_id":"R4-2520335-003","collection":"ran4_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Huawei","HiSilicon"],"tdocNumber":"R4-2520335","title":"Consideration on UE/BS RF spec improvement"},"point_id":"16303462025564108428"}
We would like to suggest to investigate the following ideas for 6G BS RF specification optimization: Core and test specifications consideration NR BS specification covers Core spec TS 38.104, as well as two test specifications for conducted and OTA testing (TS 38.141-1 and TS 38.141-2). Significant parts of those specifications are based on copy-pasting. Secondly, multiple sections among core and test specs only differ with details like, e.g., core limits vs. test limits. Therefore, we would like to investigate merging core and test specifications into a single one. A simple dummy spec can be created to depict its pros and cons. Proposal 2-1: For BS RF, consider merging core and test specifications. RF vs. demodulation requirements Referring to NR BS RF specification, it covers RF Tx, RF Rx, as well as demodulation performance requirements. RF Tx and RX Rx requirements are obviously handled by the same group of delegates. However, demodulation requirements are handled by another group of delegates. From specification rapporteur point of view, there is also a dis-connection among the technical work done on RF requirements, and on performance requirements. RF experts are not really reviewing demod CRs, and demod experts are not really reviewing RF CRs. This has created many misalignments within a single specification in the past. On specification side, the only aspect common to RF and demod is the specification of FRCs. With the above, we would like to suggest to investigate separation of demodulation requirements from RF requirements, and putting them into a separate specification. Proposal 2-2: Investigate separation of demodulation requirements from RF requirements, and putting them into a separate specification.

